{{!-- /the-faith-received/pins/ — a forward into the Research desk's
     Bookmarks tab, with the ported Notebook kept behind one query
     parameter.

     WHAT HAPPENED. There were two notebooks. This page had one, built
     on the ported engine and reading its collections out of
     localStorage under "fr_collections_v1"; the Research desk has the
     other, a Bookmarks panel reading the account's own bookmarks and a
     Notebook panel reading "fr_notebook". The rail offered both and
     they were not the same thing, which is what Ian was looking at:
     "Bookmark and Notebook in the navrail need to be the same thing as
     those on the research page." The Research desk wins, because it is
     the one wearing the site's design and the one the account's
     bookmarks are actually in. The rail's Bookmarks item now points at
     /the-faith-received/research/#bookmarks and this URL forwards there
     the same way /compare/ and /desk/ forward into their own tabs.

     THE ESCAPE HATCH, AND WHY IT EXISTS. The collections this page
     showed were never on anybody's account. They are in the reader's
     own browser and nowhere else, so there is no copy on a server to
     fall back to and no migration anyone can run on their behalf. A
     silent forward would leave a reader looking at an empty Bookmarks
     tab with their own work still sitting in localStorage two feet
     away and nothing on screen saying so. So:

       /the-faith-received/pins/                  -> /research/#bookmarks
       /the-faith-received/pins/  (with saved
         collections in this browser)             -> stays, and says so
       /the-faith-received/pins/?collections=1    -> the old view

     The parameter is the whole mechanism. It keeps the old Notebook
     reachable without keeping it in the navigation, and it costs
     nothing when nobody uses it. When the last of these collections
     has been carried across, this template becomes the three-paragraph
     forward that custom-faith-compare.hbs already is, and the shell
     below goes with it.

     WHY THE DECISION IS MADE IN A SCRIPT AND NOT IN routes.yaml. The
     condition is the contents of localStorage, which no server can
     see. routes.yaml also has to be uploaded by hand in Ghost Admin,
     so a rule there is not free. See assets/js/page/faith-pins-forward.js.

     WITHOUT SCRIPT the forward notice is the whole page and its link is
     a real link, which is the same bargain the other two forwards make.

     Source corpus page, kept inside MereO default; edits and data
     remain on the Ghost/Cloudflare port. --}}
{{#if @member}}
<div class="faith-port-pins-page">

{{!-- The header this page never had. The ported markup opened on a bar
     of its own ("The Faith Received / Theme / ‹ Library"), which was a
     fourth arrangement of links the rail already carries, and then went
     straight into the engine's own <h1>. Same .bhero as every other TFR
     landing surface, then the rail, exactly as
     custom-faith-port-search.hbs does it. The Theme button moved into
     the header below rather than being deleted: pins.in02.js binds
     #pinsTheme at its top level with no null check, and a missing
     element there throws before anything else in the file runs. --}}
<section class="bhero bhero--tool" data-pins-forward>
  <div class="bhero-inner container">
    <p class="bhero-kicker"><a href="/the-faith-received/">The Faith Received</a></p>
    <h1>Bookmarks have moved</h1>
    <p class="bhero-sub">Bookmarks and the Notebook are tabs of the Research desk now, beside Ask, Power Search, Compare and the rest. This link still works, it just takes a moment longer.</p>
    <p class="bhero-sub"><a href="/the-faith-received/research/#bookmarks">Open Bookmarks on the Research desk</a></p>

    {{!-- Shown only when this browser is holding collections that the
         old view saved. Nothing is moved and nothing is deleted; the
         reader is told where their work is and handed the door to
         it. --}}
    <div data-pins-stranded hidden>
      <p class="bhero-sub">This browser is still holding collections saved in the old notebook on this page. They were never kept on your account, only here, so nothing has been moved across for you and nothing has been thrown away.</p>
      <p class="bhero-sub"><a href="/the-faith-received/pins/?collections=1">Open your saved collections</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhero bhero--tool" data-pins-legacy-hero hidden>
  <div class="bhero-inner container">
    <p class="bhero-kicker"><a href="/the-faith-received/">The Faith Received</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> Saved collections</p>
    <h1>Saved collections</h1>
    <p class="bhero-sub">The old notebook, kept so that collections saved in this browser stay reachable. New work belongs on the Research desk, in <a href="/the-faith-received/research/#bookmarks">Bookmarks</a> and <a href="/the-faith-received/research/#notebook">Notebook</a>.</p>
    <p><button type="button" class="btn" id="pinsTheme" aria-label="Change reading theme">Theme</button></p>
  </div>
</section>

<script src="{{asset "js/page/faith-tfr-rail.js"}}" defer></script>

